<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong Motor union to resume strike.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong Motor union to resume strike.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unionised workers at Ssangyong Motor Co, a unit of South Korea's Ssangyong Group  SSYG.CN, will resume their walkout at 1:30 p.m. (0430 GMT) on Monday, a union official said.</p>
<p>The strike will affect 7,853 workers, union spokesman Park Chung-sun said. Last week, the workers temporarily suspended a strike launched in protest of the December 26 passage of a new labour law.  </p>
<p>&quot;The union will walk out this afternoon,&quot; Park said.</p>
<p>Strikes have crippled much of South Korean industry since a new labour law allowing lay-offs, flexible work hours and the replacement of striking workers was rammed through parliament on December 26.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
